You are taking part in a decision task in a group of {{ group_size }} people. It is always the same group, every round. The points you earn in all rounds are added up and paid to you as real money at the end, so every point matters to you; the same is true for the others.

In each round every group member picks a whole number from 0 to {{ max_guess }}. All members decide at the same time, without seeing the others' numbers.
The target is {{ p_text }} of the average of all {{ group_size }} numbers. The member whose number is closest to the target gets {{ prize }} points; if several members are equally close, they share the {{ prize }} points equally. Everyone else gets 0 points in that round.
